--- !u!1001 &5671592406410795253
PrefabInstance:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  serializedVersion: 2
  m_Modification:
    serializedVersion: 3
    m_TransformParent: {fileID: 4885456637723263855}
    m_Modifications:
    - target: {fileID: 4370922882536067556, guid: c328e3cd83fb5284a92c73432116a752,
        type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_text
      value: '<align=center><b>Quantum Fringe Patterns Without Interference</b><br></align><br>
        <b></b>In this world, quantum scattering simulations demonstrate how research
        by Carolyne Van Vliet and William Duane can be applied to replicate both
        single- and double-slit experiments, producing the typical fringe patterns
        without the incident particles undergoing interference. '
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
